    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0676" n="668" xml:id="pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2506</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-27">November 27, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Australia called at his request. His purpose was to inquire
                    whether the proposed <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> had been
                    abandoned permanently, to which I replied that I so considered it. He expressed
                    great concern and desired to know more about the movements of Chiang Kai-shek
                    and others intended to discourage the further consideration of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>. I referred to copies of British
                    communications on the subject, adding that Ambassador Halifax was strong for the
                    proposal all the way and that I sympathized with his situation but I did not
                    feel that the communications from Churchill and Eden, with qualifications such
                    as were in them, would be very helpful in a bitter fight that would be projected
                    by Chiang Kai-shek and carried forward by all of the malcontents in the United
                    States, although I felt unreservedly that Churchill and Eden, like the British
                    Ambassador here, would be for whatever we might do, even though not entirely to
                    their liking in every way. The Minister inquired whether I thought it would be
                    feasible to take up this matter further with the Chinese and I replied that I
                    did not think so, so far as I am concerned. I thanked the Minister for his
                    cooperation and that of his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
